Subject: [PATCH] source: add an evdev motion sensor source
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reads evdev motion sensors (INPUT_PROP_ACCELEROMETER, ID_INPUT_ACCELEROMETER):
ABS_X/Y/Z acceleration and ABS_RX/RY/RZ angular velocity in the kernel's
motion sensor frame, scaled by each axis resolution, into Accelerometer (m/s²)
and Gyroscope (rad/s) events in that same frame, the SI units and axes
InputPlumber's targets take since 0.82 (the Steam Deck target reports X, -Z, Y,
as the kernel's hid-steam driver does). For sensors without a kernel driver
that a userspace daemon exposes through uinput (Kettle Linux: kettle-motiond,
for the Qualcomm Sensor Core motion sensors on AYN handhelds), so its virtual
device, "Kettle Motion Sensors", joins the virtual device whitelist. Only
devices named in IMU_DEVICE_NAMES get this driver: other accelerometer nodes
(a DualShock 4's motion node) keep the gamepad driver.
